"content":"Here is the report formatted exactly for our continuation checkpoint:\n\n# Continuation Summary\n\n## 1. 
Outstanding User Requests\n- **Frontend Interactivity (Ongoing)**: The user requested that we make all frontend 
components and buttons interactive step-by-step in the following order: Hero Page → Dashboard → Projects → Settings. 
The Hero Page and Dashboard have been completed; Projects and Settings are pending.\n- **Third-Party API Integrations 
(Pending)**: The user requested the integration of MindMeister, XMind, and Coggle APIs once the core frontend pages 
are fully interactive.\n- **Backend Enhancements (Pending)**: The backend architecture needs significant upgrades 
(WebSockets for real-time collaboration, new database schemas for prioritization and presentation mode) after the 
frontend is completed.\n\n## 2. User Knowledge\n- **Project Scope/Rules**: \"I am building the web using you, I have 
to learn from this, then only I can understand this project and I can explain this to someone. So side by side explain 
what we done in every task.\"\n- **Workflow**: Progress through the application systematically. Do not make many 
unrelated changes at once. Verify functionality before moving to the next task.\n- **Project Specifications**: The app 
aims to support text-to-mindmap, auto-expansion, connection discovery, prioritization (highlighting important nodes), 
presentation mode, real-time collaboration, and exports to PDF/image.\n\n## 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Backend 
Architecture Review**: Analyzed the FastAPI structure against the advanced specs. Identified missing requirements: 
WebSockets (for collaboration), presentation order logic, node importance scoring, and OAuth services. Decided to 
postpone backend upgrades until the frontend is interactive.\n- **Hero Page (Landing) Interactivity**:\n  - 
Implemented dynamic authentication checks in the header (`index.tsx`). If `access_token` exists, \"Sign In\" is hidden 
and the CTA becomes \"Go to Dashboard\".\n  - Transformed the static AI prompt mockup into an interactive funnel. 
Typi\n<truncated 340 bytes>\n` and `createMindMap`, then seamlessly route the user to `/workspace?mindMapId=...`.\n  - 
Implemented logic to intercept `pending_ai_prompt` from the Hero page, automatically provision a project, and forward 
the topic to the workspace.\n- **Workspace Search Schema**: Updated the TanStack router schema in `workspace.tsx` to 
accept an optional `?topic=` parameter, enabling the prompt funnel from the landing page to auto-fill the AI 
generation bar.\n\n## 4. Model Knowledge\n- **API Flow for Project Creation**: When building UI flows, a \"Project\" 
acts as a folder. To get a user into the canvas, we must first `createProject()`, then immediately 
`createMindMap(projectId)`, and finally route to `/workspace?mindMapId={id}`.\n- **React Router State Hand-off**: We 
use a combination of `localStorage` (for bouncing across protected route boundaries like the login wall) and URL 
search parameters (`?topic=`) to successfully carry user intent from the unauthenticated landing page directly into 
the workspace canvas.\n\n## 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited Files (Recent)**\n  - `C:\\AI 
Mindmap\\frontend\\src\\routes\\index.tsx`: Replaced static landing buttons with dynamic auth state. Converted mockup 
`<div>` into an interactive `<form>` that saves `pending_ai_prompt`.\n  - `C:\\AI 
Mindmap\\frontend\\src\\routes\\dashboard.tsx`: Replaced hardcoded `STATS` and `PROJECTS` arrays with live API calls. 
Added `handleCreateProject` logic and `pending_ai_prompt` interceptor.\n  - `C:\\AI 
Mindmap\\frontend\\src\\routes\\workspace.tsx`: Updated `validateSearch` to include `topic: string` and initialized 
the `topic` React state using this URL parameter.\n\n## 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- **Current Status**: The 
backend analysis is complete. The Hero Page and Dashboard are now fully interactive, successfully fetching live data 
and connecting via an AI prompt funnel.\n- **Next Step**: Move on to the **Projects** page (`/projects`) and the 
**Settings** page (`/settings`) to implement their specific interactive actions, followed by planning the Third-Party 
API integrations.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
